{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011aKFzfSncr5BiAsB4MDW3s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough context. Let me implement the changes:\n\n1. **fileinfo.go** - The current Stat/Lstat already wrap errors from os.Stat/os.Lstat properly (they return the error directly). The errors from os.Stat/os.Lstat already support os.IsNotExist and os.IsPermission. For R1.6 (fallback when no syscall.Stat_t), I need to handle the case where unix.Stat fails but os.Stat succeeds - populate from os.FileInfo only. \n\nFor R1.7, Lstat already uses os.Lstat which doesn't follow symlinks, so that's handled correctly. Let me review the requirements again: I need to ensure Stat/Lstat handle errors gracefully with proper wrapping, populate available fields from os.FileInfo when syscall.Stat_t isn't available, make sure Lstat on symlinks captures the symlink's own metadata with the ModeSymlink flag set, and implement TerminalWidth using the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl. Looking at the existing code, Stat and Lstat are already returning os.Stat errors directly, which is good for error checking.\n\nThe issue is that there's a second unix.Stat call that could fail independently—if that fails but os.Stat succeeds, I should fall back to populating FileInfo from just the os.FileInfo fields. Lstat is already using os.Lstat which gives symlink metadata, and since populateFileInfo uses info.Mode(), it'll correctly include ModeSymlink for symlinks.\n\nI need to add a fallback path in Stat and Lstat that handles the case where unix.Stat fails, then move on to implementing TerminalWidth and IsTerminal in terminal.go.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3077,"cache_read_input_tokens":72220,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3077},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"